{
  "comment": "Byte-stability fixtures for the Seatbelt profile compiler. Every path is an absolute path under a directory that exists on no host (/_sbparity), so canonicalization resolves the longest existing prefix (/) and re-appends the tail lexically — byte-identical output on every machine. These began as Go-compiler parity goldens (internal/seatbelt, deleted in P4); Go parity is RETIRED as of the ro-hole emission (rsc-w0z) — the Go compiler only ever emitted allows. The TS compiler in ../profile.ts is the implementation of record; the goldens now pin ITS output. Regenerate with the goldengen note in goldens.json.",
